<title>UK: British Energy to axe 1,300 jobs - paper.</title>
<headline>British Energy to axe 1,300 jobs - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Energy, the recently privatised nuclear power generator, will unveil plans to cut 1,300 jobs to trim costs and maintain its policy of growing dividends, the Guardian newspaper reported on Monday.</p>
<p>The jobs will be slashed at the company's English and Welsh operations, but further job losses are expected in the near future at the Scottish operations too, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
